These are concrete vaulted tanks.&nbsp; There are two (2) separate vaults each with a steel tank inside that is split in two (2 tanks per vault).&nbsp; The larger vault contains 2 tanks ... 2,500 gallon capacity each, and the smaller vault contains 2 tanks with 1,000 gallon capacity each.

Each tank has its own pump and retracting hose assembly upright that keeps the hose off the ground.&nbsp; The 1,000 gallon tanks had gasoline in one and Dyed Low Sulfur Diesel (non-taxable) in the other (both currently empty but not dry).&nbsp; The 2,500 gallon tanks have Clear Low Sulfur Diesel (taxed) in them, one of which is empty (not dry) and the other has approximately 1,500 gallons still in it.&nbsp; We can have our vendor pump out the tanks completely prior to relocating them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

For more information, contact Jeff Bohne at (708) 267-9006

